{"Adding a new abstract method `int order()` to the public `CryptoProvider` interface is a binary-incompatible change that will cause `AbstractMethodError` at runtime for any existing third-party implementations not updated in this PR": 0.9410626292228699, "CryptoIntegration.init called with AuthzClient's classloader may cause ServiceLoader to find only the Authz-client-local provider and not providers available via parent or application classloaders": 0.6936638951301575, "CryptoIntegration.init stores the chosen provider in a static volatile singleton that is never changed, so if invoked early with narrow classloader visibility, the system will be locked to that provider even if a more capable provider is available later": 0.8591058850288391, "ASN1Decoder.readLength() returns -1 for indefinite-length encoding, which can make computed length negative when passed to read(int), causing NegativeArraySizeException or crash from new byte[length] without negativity check": 0.916576623916626, "Crafted DER/ASN.1 input with indefinite-length encodings or malformed lengths can trigger exceptions during parsing and crash the client or consume resources (DoS)": 0.6500388979911804, "AuthzClientCryptoProvider is registered as a CryptoProvider via META-INF/services but most of its methods throw UnsupportedOperationException, which would break any caller relying on those capabilities": 0.5559661984443665, "ServiceLoader provider selection now silently prefers highest 'order' provider, allowing an attacker or misconfiguration to place a CryptoProvider with higher order value that will be preferred automatically and used globally": 0.3227117955684662, "Malicious crypto provider selection is silent (ignored providers only logged at DEBUG), so operators may not notice a non-default provider is being used": 0.3777049481868744}